"terms_accept" = "I have read and accept the terms and conditions";
"terms_content" = "TERMS AND CONDITIONS\nAttack On Anaphylaxis\nLast updated: November 26, 2025\n\n1. IDENTIFICATION OF THE RESPONSIBLE PARTY\nResponsible: Colegio Nacional de Inmunología Clínica y Alergia de México, A.C. (CMICA)\nDevelopers: Tecnológico de Monterrey\n* Alejandra Salgado Garcia\n* Carla Ivette Duval López\n* Gabriel Alejandro Palomino López\n* Carolina Elizondo Martínez\nAddress: [Complete CMICA Address]\nRFC: [CMICA RFC]\nContact: [Official Email]\nPhone: [Support Phone]\nWebsite: [Official Website]\n\n2. NATURE AND SCOPE OF THE APPLICATION\n2.1 Definition of the Application\nAttack On Anaphylaxis is an educational and informational tool designed exclusively to:\n* Help children aged 6 to 12 understand their food allergies through interactive games\n* Teach identification of foods containing allergens through personalized game levels\n* Provide educational stories teaching recognition of signs and symptoms of allergic reactions\n* Offer general information about allergies validated by CMICA in child-appropriate language\n2.2 Limitations of the Application\nTHIS APPLICATION IS NOT:\n* A certified medical device\n* A medical diagnostic service\n* A medical emergency system\n* A substitute for professional medical care\n* A tool for making critical medical decisions\n* A hospital location service\nThe application is solely a playful-educational learning tool.\n2.3 Complementary Nature\nAttack On Anaphylaxis is an educational support tool that complements, but DOES NOT substitute:\n* Professional medical consultation\n* Medical diagnosis by a certified allergist\n* Prescribed medical treatment\n* Instructions from your treating physician\n* Emergency protocols established by health professionals\nThe user acknowledges and accepts that the application provides informative content based on information validated by CMICA, but each allergy case is unique and requires individualized medical supervision.\n\n3. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n3.1 Medical Liability\nCMICA, Tecnológico de Monterrey, and the developers assume NO liability for:\na) Medical decisions made based on application information\nb) Delays in seeking professional medical attention\nc) Worsening of health conditions due to improper use of the application\nd) Allergic reactions not prevented or identified through use of the application\ne) Consequences derived from relying exclusively on educational stories to identify real allergic reactions\n3.2 Educational-Playful Nature\nThe application uses allergen identification games, educational stories, and personalized levels. These elements are EDUCATIONAL SIMULATIONS and:\n* Do not replace formal medical education\n* Do not guarantee the child will correctly identify a real reaction\n* Require reinforcement by parents and doctors\n* May not cover all presentations of allergic reactions\n3.3 Accuracy of Information\nAlthough information has been validated by CMICA:\n* Each allergy case is unique and may present differently\n* Information is simplified for child comprehension\n* It does not substitute specific instructions from your doctor\n* Real symptoms may vary from those shown in stories\n3.4 Technical Functionality\nWe are not responsible for:\n* Technical failures of the user's device\n* Incompatibility with operating systems\n* Loss of locally stored data, including child profile and progress\n* Temporary unavailability of application functions\n* Errors or defects in the game affecting the experience\n3.5 Educational Use, NOT Emergency\nTHE USER EXPRESSLY ACKNOWLEDGES THAT:\n* This application MUST NOT be used during a real medical emergency\n* In case of anaphylactic shock or severe reaction, call 911 IMMEDIATELY\n* Educational stories are for preventive learning, not for real-time diagnosis\n* Knowledge acquired through the game must be complemented with professional medical education\n3.6 Maximum Liability Limit\nIn case any liability is determined, it is limited to the amount paid by the user for use of the application. Being a free application, said amount is zero pesos ($0.00 MXN), excluding in any case indirect, consequential, or punitive damages.\n\n4. USER OBLIGATIONS\n4.1 Mandatory Medical Consultation\nThe user, parent, or legal guardian agrees to:\nBEFORE USING THE APPLICATION:\n* Have a professional medical diagnosis of the minor's allergies\n* Have consulted with a certified allergist\n* Have an allergy management plan prescribed by a doctor\n* Have prescribed emergency medications\nDURING USE OF THE APPLICATION:\n* Supervise the minor's use of the application\n* Verify that entered information is correct according to medical diagnosis\n* NOT substitute regular medical consultations with application use\n* Keep the allergy action plan updated with their doctor\nNEVER USE THE APPLICATION TO:\n* Self-diagnose allergies\n* Decide if emergency medical attention is required\n* Determine treatments or medication doses\n* Suspend prescribed medications\n* Delay seeking professional medical attention\nCRITICAL WARNING: Use of this application without adequate professional medical supervision may put the minor's health at risk. Parents or guardians are solely responsible for ensuring the minor receives appropriate medical care for their allergies.\n\n5. SPECIFIC WARNINGS FOR USE BY MINORS\n5.1 Mandatory Parental Supervision\n* This application MUST be used under supervision of a responsible adult\n* Parents or guardians must configure the child's profile and allergy type\n* The minor MUST NOT make medical decisions based on the application\n* Parents must verify the child understands it is an EDUCATIONAL GAME\n5.2 Nature of Content\nThe game teaches identification of allergen foods playfully and stories show examples of symptom presentation. However:\n* REAL symptoms can be different in each person\n* They MUST NOT use the application to diagnose if they are having a reaction\n5.3 Difference Between Game and Reality\nChildren must clearly understand that:\n* In the game they identify foods to avoid\n* In real life, if they eat something wrong they must inform an ADULT immediately\n* Stories show characters with symptoms to LEARN to recognize them\n* If THEY have real symptoms they must seek adult help, NOT check the application\n5.4 Complementary Education\n* Parents must reinforce teachings with real medical information\n* The child's doctor should know they use this educational application\n* Some concepts may require additional explanation by adults\n* The game DOES NOT cover all possible allergy situations\n5.5 Device Use\n* Screen time must be controlled by parents\n* The application requires basic reading, designed for children who can read\n* May require assistance for complex functions or configuration\n* Does not require internet connection, works offline\n5.6 For Parents and Guardians\nWHAT THE APPLICATION CAN DO:\n* Teach through games which foods to avoid\n* Show through stories what different symptoms look like\n* Reinforce knowledge about their child's allergies\n* Create awareness in the child about their condition\nWHAT THE APPLICATION CANNOT DO:\n* Diagnose allergies, which requires a doctor\n* Identify reactions in real-time\n* Substitute an allergy action plan\n* Contact emergency services\n* Guide treatment during a reaction\n* Guarantee the child will react correctly in a real emergency\nIMPORTANT NOTE: The current version of \"Attack On Anaphylaxis\" is designed EXCLUSIVELY for children aged 6 to 12. Use by other age groups is not contemplated in this version and is done under the user's complete responsibility.\n\n6. MINOR USERS AND DATA PROTECTION\n6.1 Applicable Legal Framework\nAccording to the Federal Law on Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties (LFPDPPP) and its Regulations:\n* Obtaining consent from the parent or legal guardian is mandatory\n* Consent must be express, informed, and written\n* Health or allergy-related data are considered sensitive personal data\n* Express and separate consent from the guardian is required for sensitive data\n* The owner may revoke consent at any time\n6.2 Reinforced Protection\nStrict administrative, technical, and physical security measures are implemented:\n* Data transfer without explicit consent is prohibited\n* The minor's preferential right to be forgotten is recognized\n* Data cannot be used for profiling or advertising without special consent\n* Parents or guardians may exercise ARCO rights on behalf of the minor\n6.3 Parental Consent\nBy configuring the application, you declare and accept that:\n[ ] I am the parent or legal guardian of the minor using this application\n[ ] I have read and accept the Terms and Conditions in their entirety\n[ ] I authorize local storage of my child's health data, specifically the type of food allergies\n[ ] I understand this application is educational and DOES NOT substitute professional medical care\n[ ] I accept as legal guardian and provide my express consent for the treatment of the minor's sensitive health data\n\n7. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n7.1 Copyright\nAll elements of the application are protected by Federal Copyright Law:\n* Source code and software architecture\n* Adaptive level system and original game mechanics\n* Visual content: interface design, illustrations, characters, graphics, animations, and sprites\n* Educational stories, narratives, and story mode scripts\n* Adapted educational content and gamification methodology\n* Food database and classification\n* \"Attack On Anaphylaxis\" logo and brand\nOwnership: Tecnológico de Monterrey as work for hire. Base medical information: Colegio Nacional de Inmunología Clínica y Alergia de México, A.C. (CMICA). Duration: 100 years from first publication\n7.2 Trademark Registration\nThe trade name \"Attack On Anaphylaxis\" and its logo are subject to registration with the Mexican Institute of Industrial Property (IMPI).\n7.3 Permitted Uses\nThe user is authorized exclusively for:\nPERSONAL AND EDUCATIONAL:\n* Installing the application on personal devices of their family unit\n* Use by the minor under their supervision\n* Creating profiles for their children or dependents\n* Using for educational purposes regarding food allergies\n* Sharing personal experience with the application on social networks\n* Recommending the application to other parents\n7.4 Expressly Prohibited Uses\nThe user is NOT authorized to:\nMODIFICATION AND DISTRIBUTION:\n* Decompile, reverse engineer, or disassemble the application\n* Modify, adapt, or create derivative works of the software\n* Remove, alter, or hide copyright or trademark notices\n* Distribute, sublicense, or resell the application\n* Upload the application to alternative stores or unofficial repositories\n* Create modified versions of the application\nUNAUTHORIZED COMMERCIAL USE:\n* Use the application for commercial purposes without express license\n* Integrate the application into third-party commercial products or services\n* Charge for access or use of the application\n* Offer the application as part of a paid service package\n* Use application content in commercial marketing materials\nCONTENT EXTRACTION:\n* Extract, copy, or reuse graphics, illustrations, or visual designs\n* Extract, copy, or reuse educational stories or narratives\n* Extract, copy, or reuse food and allergen database\n* Extract, copy, or reuse medical information provided by CMICA\n* Extract, copy, or reuse game mechanics or educational methodology\n* Create competing applications based on our content\n* Use screenshots or videos of the application without proper attribution\nDATA MISUSE:\n* Attempt to access other users' data\n* Use hacking techniques to extract database information\n* Share or publish minor's information without consent\n* Perform data mining or unauthorized analysis\n* Link the application with unauthorized tracking services\nIMPERSONATION AND COUNTERFEITING:\n* Impersonate a developer or official representative\n* Create fake websites or social media for the application\n* Distribute counterfeit versions or malware\n* Use the brand to deceive or confuse users\nINAPPROPRIATE MEDICAL USE:\n* Use the application as a substitute for medical diagnosis\n* Base treatment decisions solely on the application\n* Promote the application as a certified medical device\n* Use during real medical emergencies instead of calling 911\n* Offer the application as a solution to symptoms without medical supervision\nINAPPROPRIATE CONTENT:\n* Introduce malware, viruses, or malicious code\n* Attempt to overload or disrupt operation\n* Use the application to transmit illegal content\n* Manipulate the application for uses unrelated to allergies\n7.5 Consequences of Misuse\nMisuse of the application may result in:\nIMMEDIATE MEASURES:\n* Temporary or permanent suspension of access\n* Deactivation of specific functionalities\n* Removal of infringing content\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\nFor Intellectual Property infringements:\n* Lawsuit for copyright violation under Federal Copyright Law\n* Compensation for economic damages\n* Fines up to 20,000 days of minimum wage under Article 229 of the LFDA\n* Imprisonment from 6 months to 6 years in severe cases\nFor unauthorized commercial use:\n* Cease and desist commercial activities\n* Compensation for illegally obtained profits\n* Legal costs and expenses\nFor brand impersonation:\n* Actions before the Mexican Institute of Industrial Property (IMPI) for trademark infringement\n* Compensation for damages to brand reputation\n\n8. PRIVACY AND PERSONAL DATA PROTECTION\n8.1 Data We Collect\nSENSITIVE HEALTH DATA:\n* Type or types of minor's food allergy (example: peanut, egg, dairy allergy, etc.)\nNON-SENSITIVE PERSONAL DATA:\n* Minor's name\n* Minor's age\n* Guardian's name (optional)\n* Guardian's email (optional)\n8.2 Purposes of Data Processing\nPRIMARY PURPOSES (necessary for service operation):\nA. Educational game personalization\n* Adapt game levels according to allergy type\n* Show foods relevant to the specific allergy of the minor\n* Personalize educational stories about symptoms\nB. Basic application operation\n* Registration of boy or girl profile\n* Save game progress\n* Show age-appropriate educational content\nC. Compliance with medical validation\n* Present information validated by CMICA according to registered allergy\nConsent for these purposes is granted by accepting the initial Privacy Notice and is necessary for application operation.\nSECONDARY PURPOSES (improve experience but are NOT essential):\nA. Usage reminder notifications\n* Send notifications to encourage continuous use of the application\n* Reminders to complete educational levels\nB. User experience improvement\n* Local analysis of usage patterns\n* Difficulty adjustment according to performance\nConsent for these purposes is requested separately and MAY be denied without affecting the main operation of the application.\n8.3 What We DO NOT Do with Data\n* WE DO NOT diagnose or replace medical consultation\n* WE DO NOT share data with third parties, including CMICA, developers, or any other entity\n* WE DO NOT send data to external servers or internet\n* WE DO NOT use data for medical or scientific research\n* WE DO NOT use data for statistics or advertising\n* WE DO NOT track location or device information\n* WE DO NOT perform user profiling\n8.4 Storage and Security\nDATA LOCATION: Allergy data and all personal information are stored solely on the mobile device where the application was installed, in an encrypted local database (SQLite with AES-256 encryption).\nNeither developers nor the CMICA organization have access to this data at any time.\nTECHNICAL SECURITY MEASURES:\nA. Secure Storage\n* Database encrypted with SQLite using AES-256 encryption\n* Local storage: Data NEVER leaves the device\n* No internet connection: The application works completely offline for personal data\nB. Access Control\n* Device protection: It is recommended to activate screen lock with PIN or fingerprint\n* No user authentication on servers: There are no passwords that can be compromised\n* Minimal permissions: The application only requests strictly necessary permissions\nC. Data Integrity\n* Validation via hashing: We detect if data was modified without authorization\n* Automatic local backup: Encrypted backup on the device\n* Input validation: We prevent malicious data injection\nD. Malware Protection\n* Clean architecture: Modular code facilitating security audits\n* No unverified third-party libraries: Reduces attack vectors\n* Security updates: We publish patches when vulnerabilities are detected\nADMINISTRATIVE SECURITY MEASURES:\nA. Access Policies\n* Principle of least privilege in development team\n* Confidentiality agreements signed by the whole team\n* Separation of roles: Developers do not have access to user data\nB. Personnel Management\n* Data protection training according to LFPDPPP\n* Documented incident response protocol\nC. Secure Development Life Cycle\n* Code review before each update\n* Security testing against common vulnerabilities\n* Security architecture documentation\n8.5 Retention Period\nData remains on the device until:\n* You uninstall the application\n* You use the \"Delete profile\" option in settings\n* You restore the device to factory settings\n8.6 Data Transfers\nAttack On Anaphylaxis DOES NOT perform personal data transfers:\nWHAT DOES HAPPEN:\n* Data saved locally on your phone or tablet\n* Encryption on the same device\n* Local backups if the user configures them manually\nWHAT DOES NOT HAPPEN:\n* WE DO NOT send data to internet servers\n* WE DO NOT use cloud services like AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, or similar\n* NO cloud synchronization\n* Developers DO NOT have access to your child's data\n* CMICA DOES NOT receive user data\nOFFLINE OPERATION: The application works completely without internet connection for personal data handling. The only connection might be to:\n* Download application updates from App Store or Google Play\n* Validate updated medical information from CMICA, without sending user data\nTOTAL CONTROL: You have absolute control of the data because it is on YOUR device. You can delete it at any time from application settings or by uninstalling the application.\n8.7 International Transfers\nAttack On Anaphylaxis DOES NOT perform international data transfers because all storage is local on the user's device.\n8.8 Use of Validated Medical Information\nEducational information about allergies presented in the game is validated by the Colegio Mexicano de Inmunología Clínica y Alergia (CMICA). However, your personal information IS NOT shared with them at any time.\n\n9. ARCO RIGHTS\n9.1 Your Rights\nAs owner of personal data or legal guardian of the minor, you have the right to:\nACCESS: Access data we have about your child\nRECTIFICATION: Rectify incorrect or incomplete data\nCANCELLATION: Cancel or delete data when no longer necessary\nOPPOSITION: Oppose data processing for specific purposes\nREVOCATION: Revoke your consent at any time\nLIMITATION: Limit the use or disclosure of personal data\n9.2 Exercise of ARCO Rights\nBecause all data is stored locally on your device:\nTO ACCESS DATA:\n* Enter the \"Settings\" or \"Profile\" section within the application\nTO RECTIFY DATA:\n* Enter the \"Settings\" or \"Profile\" section and modify necessary information\nTO CANCEL OR DELETE DATA:\n* Use the \"Delete profile\" option in application settings, or\n* Uninstall the application from your device\nTO OPPOSE OR LIMIT USE:\n* Configure notification preferences in the settings section\n* Deactivate secondary functionalities according to your preferences\nTO REVOKE CONSENT:\n* Delete the minor's profile from settings, or\n* Uninstall the application\n9.3 Identity Verification\nThe application has no functionality for a third party to access user health data. Access control is based on physical control of the mobile device.\n9.4 Response Times\nIn case of formal requests to the