o 12 years with parental supervision\n\n12. REGULATIONS AND LEGAL COMPLIANCE\n12.1 Mexican Legal Framework\nThis application operates in compliance with:\n* Federal Law on Protection of Personal Data Held by Private Parties (LFPDPPP)\n* Regulations of the LFPDPPP\n* Federal Consumer Protection Law (LFPC)\n* Federal Copyright Law (LFDA)\n* General Health Law (LGS)\n* Official Mexican Standard NOM-004-SSA3-2012\n12.2 International Standards\nAlthough this application is designed exclusively for use in Mexico, it adheres to international best practice standards:\n* Privacy by Design principles\n* Data security standards\n* Health application development best practices\n12.3 No HIPAA Applicability\nThis application IS NOT subject to the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) of the United States because:\n* We are not a covered entity (health provider, insurer)\n* We do not transmit health information to providers\n* We do not process insurance claims\n* Data IS NOT shared with third parties\n\n13. UPDATES AND MODIFICATIONS\n13.1 Modifications to Terms and Conditions\nWe reserve the right to modify these Terms and Conditions at any time. Changes will be notified via:\n* Pop-up notice in the application with summary of changes\n* Notification to email if provided\n* Publication of updated version with last modification date\n13.2 Transition Period for Substantial Changes\nFor substantial changes in terms:\n* A period of 30 calendar days will be granted to accept new terms\n* During this period, the previous version of functionalities will be maintained\n* If you do not accept changes, only new or affected secondary functionalities will be deactivated\n* Essential educational functionalities will remain available\n13.3 Acceptance of Changes\nContinued use of the application after the transition period constitutes acceptance of new terms.\n13.4 New Functionalities\nAny new functionality requiring:\n* Processing of additional data\n* New device permissions\n* Changes in data processing purposes\nWill require your explicit consent via pop-up notice before activation.\nIf you do not accept new functionalities, these will remain disabled, but you can continue using existing functionalities.\n13.5 Security Updates\nSecurity updates and bug fixes will be implemented automatically through application stores (App Store and Google Play) according to your automatic update settings.\n\n14. ALLIANCES AND COLLABORATIONS\n14.1 Collaboration with CMICA\nThis application has been developed in collaboration with the Colegio Nacional de Inmunología Clínica y Alergia de México, A.C. (CMICA), which:\n* Validates medical content presented in the application\n* Provides scientific information on food allergies\n* Supervises accuracy of educational information on symptoms\nHowever, CMICA:\n* DOES NOT receive personal user data\n* DOES NOT have access to information stored on user devices\n* IS NOT responsible for technical operation of the application\n14.2 Use of Validated Information\nMedical information presented has been validated by certified professionals. However:\n* Information is simplified for child comprehension\n* Each case is unique and requires individual medical evaluation\n* Information may be updated according to new medical knowledge\n\n15. TERMINATION AND SUSPENSION\n15.1 Termination by User\nThe user may terminate use of the application at any time by:\n* Uninstalling the application from their device\n* Deleting the profile from settings\n* Ceasing use of the application\n15.2 Suspension for Non-Compliance\nWe reserve the right to:\n* Suspend access to the application in case of misuse\n* Block specific functionalities if violation of these terms is detected\n* Take legal action in case of severe infringements\n15.3 Effects of Termination\nUpon terminating use:\n* Locally stored data will remain on your device until you manually delete it\n* There is no obligation to keep backups by developers\n* Any technical support or attention related to the application will cease\n\n16. GEOGRAPHIC LIMITATIONS\n16.1 Scope of Application\nThis application is designed and adapted exclusively for use in the United Mexican States.\n16.2 International Use Limitations\n* Content is in Spanish and English\n* Information standards follow Mexican protocols\n* References to emergency services use Mexico's 911 number\n* Date formats and cultural conventions are Mexican\n* Regulatory compliance is oriented to Mexican legislation\n16.3 Use Outside Mexico\nUse of this application outside Mexican territory:\n* Is not contemplated in the current design\n* Is done under the user's complete responsibility\n* May not comply with local regulations of other countries\n* May present information not applicable to other medical or cultural contexts\n\n17. GENERAL PROVISIONS\n17.1 Entire Agreement\nThese Terms and Conditions, together with the Privacy Notice, constitute the entire agreement between the user and those responsible for the application.\n17.2 Severability\nIf any provision of these terms is declared invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by competent authority, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.\n17.3 Waiver\nThe lack of exercise or application of any right or provision of these terms shall not constitute a waiver of said right or provision.\n17.4 Language\nIn case of versions in other languages, the Spanish version shall prevail in case of conflict or discrepancy.\n17.5 Assignment\nThe user may not assign or transfer their rights or obligations under these terms without prior written consent. Those responsible may assign these terms without restriction.\n17.6 Contact and Notifications\nFor any doubt, comment, or notification related to these Terms and Conditions:\nEmail: [contact email]\nPrivacy Officer: Carolina Elizondo Martínez\nAddress: [Complete Address]\nPhone: [Support Phone]\n17.7 Jurisdiction and Applicable Law\nThese Terms and Conditions are governed by the laws 